# Methods

The manuscript was written as Markdown sections under
`manuscript/main/`. The sections were concatenated in filename order and
expanded by trazo before Pandoc was called ([@fig:workflow]). Include
directives inserted the generated tables, and `{{v:key}}` placeholders
were replaced by numbers computed from the data by
`scripts/build_values.py`, so no number in the prose was typed by hand.

![[Build workflow of the example paper.]{.caption-title} Sections are expanded (includes and computed values), rendered by Pandoc with citations and cross-references, and written to Word.](figures/external/fig2_workflow.png){#fig:workflow width=100%}

The example figure and table were generated with Python scripts that use
only the standard library. The table numbers were computed by
`tables/scripts/generate_tables.py` and formatted by trazo with the
table spec in `tables/specs/`. Citation keys were checked
against `bibliography/references.bib` before the Word document was
accepted.

Scores were summarised with their mean and standard deviation (SD).

